        "original_id": "923fb063-f730-58ca-9362-18531f5dc7c8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Jackson, Bob Giraldi, Quincy Jones\n- Works: \"Beat It\", Thriller, E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial, \"Dinner Rush\"\n- Places: Westlake Recording Studios, Los Angeles\n- Companies: MCA Records\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Jackson's sixth solo album Thriller was released in 1982.\n- Recording sessions for Thriller took place from April to November 1982 at Westlake Recording Studios in Los Angeles, and the album had a production budget of $750,000.\n- \"Beat It\" is a song written and performed by American singer Michael Jackson, and it was released as a single from Thriller.\n- The album E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial was narrated by Michael Jackson, produced by Quincy Jones, and distributed by MCA Records.\n- Bob Giraldi was born on January 17, 1939.\n- Bob Giraldi is an American film and television director known for directing the film \"Dinner Rush\" and the music video for Michael Jackson's song \"Beat It\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
